---
title: Potato pizza
servings: 1
yield: 1 pizza
tags: [italian, vegetarian]
cuisine: italian
source: Potato Pizza by StarChefs, https://www.starchefs.com/recipes/potato-pizza
---

== Dough ==

Mix the @flour{300%g}, @whole wheat flour{53%g}, @sourdough starter{35%g}(levain)
and @salt{11%g} in a bowl. Work in the @olive oil{4%g} and @water{250%g} by
hand until the dough comes together.

Move it to an oiled bowl, cover, and let it double.

Turn it onto a floured counter, press out the air, and knead until smooth. Wrap
and refrigerate.

== Tomato sauce ==

Blend the @whole peeled tomatoes{} in a #blender{} until smooth.

== Potatoes ==

Cover the @waxy potatoes{5}(such as Nicola, thinly sliced) with water and soak
~{1%hour}. Drain.

== Pizza ==

Heat the oven with a #pizza stone{} to 500°F.

Stretch 380 g of the dough into a 14-inch round on a floured counter. Spread
2 oz of the tomato sauce over it, then add the @mozzarella{170%g},
@parmesan{56%g}, the potatoes and the @onion{1/2}(sliced).

Bake ~{13%minutes}, until the crust is charred in spots and the potatoes are
tender. Finish with @oregano{}(fresh leaves) and @flaky salt{}.
